    "lawCode": "Add §13.12, Pks & Rec L",
    "lawSection": "Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S809\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the parks, recreation and historic preservation law, in\nrelation to prohibiting littering on state park lands\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo create a greater deterrent to littering in State Parks and Historic\nSites.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n-Codifies Selection 375.1 of the Office of Parks, Recreation and Histor-\nic Preservation Codes, Rules and Regulations by prohibiting the throwing\nof refuse on park lands.\n\n-Makes appropriate exemptions for the reasonable use of ashes, sand,\nsalt or other material for the purpose of reducing the hazard. of, or\nproviding traction on snow, ice or sleet.\n\n-Creates a fine structure for the act of littering in State Parks or\nHistoric Sites, including a fine not to exceed $350 and/or community\nservice at a State Park for a first violation and a fine not to exceed\n$700 and/or community service at a State Park for a second violation.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York's State Parks are among the most magnificent in the Nation.  By\nenacting stringent policies to protect. our parks, we will deter litter-\ning and ensure our park staff spends less time picking up trash and more\ntime maintaining and beautifying parks in other ways.  Moreover, in the\nevent that someone does litter, a punishment. of community service will\nhelp maintain the tarnished park.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: S.1405 - Passed Senate\n\n2019-2020: S.2494- Passed Senate 61-0\n\n2018: S.3053-Passed Senate 62-0\n\n2017: S.3053- Passed Senate 62-0\n\n2016: S.956-Passed Senate 60-0\n\n2015: S.956-,Passed Senate 62-0\n\n2014: S.3014- Passed Senate 57-0\n\n2013: S.3014- Referred to Cultural Affairs, Tourism,Parks and Recreation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:.\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
